PATCH 609: the damage record and the attacker reach b274 as near offsets -- bd09's roll, bbb7's
[0xe3b2].

board:0017.  bd09, the structure's damage handler (asm 0xbd09-0xbd68), calls b274 with BX = the
per-state record `word[byte[di+0x19]*2 - 0x6119] + ax` -- a DGROUP near offset, which b274 (patch
493) takes as one; the port passed a host pointer whose low half named a garbage record, so the
roll's magnitude was random and `shr al,2` was modelled on the roll's 16 bits instead of AL.  bbb7
(`mov [0xe3b2],di ; mov si,[0x9a25] ; call c31e`) stores the ATTACKER's near offset for b274's side
test (`mov si,[0xe3b2] ; testb [si+0x16],8` picks the damage scale); patch 516 subtracted the
DGROUP base from a value only b5e7 passed as a host pointer, so the rocket's, the child's and the
9c76 callers' hits left a garbage attacker there.  On SAUDI1's replay the structure at 0xa090
survived the rocket that destroys it in the original (step 5848); with 609 the 17777 sim steps of
that capture match to the last draw and the object tables differ nowhere.

